-- title:
--   Geometric mod-3 forms of even weight are reductions
-- statement:
--   Let $N'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $3$ and admitting a prime divisor $q$ with $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$, let $F$ be a field of characteristic $3$, and let $m$ be a natural number. Let $G$ be an element of the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC F N'`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L61) of the Laurent series field $F((q))$, that is, of the subfield generated over $F$ by the series `jqModC F` and its $N'$-fold expansion `jqNModC F N'`, and suppose that $G$, viewed as a Laurent series, satisfies [`ModularCurve.IsModPFormFn F m`](def/ModularCurve_ModPFormFn.html#L20): the element $G^{6}\, j^{4m}(j-1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $F$-subalgebra generated by $j =$ `jqModC F`, and $G^{2}\, j^{m}(j-1728)^{m}$ is integral over the $F$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$. Then there is a power series $\varphi \in F[[q]]$ lying in `modPMod N' (2 * m) F` — the $F$-span of the series $\sum_n \bar a_n q^n$ obtained from modular forms $f$ of weight $2m$ on $\Gamma_0(N')$ whose $q$-expansion coefficients are the integers $a_n$, reduced into $F$ — whose image in $F((q))$ equals $G \cdot \vartheta_j^{\,m}$, where $\vartheta_j =$ `thetaJ F` is `thetaL F` applied to `jqModC F`. In contrast with the version cited in the proof, no algebraic closedness of $F$ is assumed and $m = 0$ is permitted.
--
--   This is the lifting step at the prime $3$: on levels prime to $3$ possessing a prime divisor $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$ — equivalently, those for which no relevant wild automorphism occurs at the supersingular points in characteristic $3$ — every geometric mod-$3$ form of even weight, presented through the two integrality conditions over $F[j]$ and $F[j^{-1}]$, has $q$-expansion coming from an $F$-combination of reductions of characteristic-zero forms of weight $2m$ on $\Gamma_0(N')$. It is used in the passage from geometric mod-$3$ data to classical mod-$3$ forms, via [`ModPForms.mem_modPMod_of_coe_mul_thetaJ_pow_eq_of_forall_ord_pos_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two`](thm.html#ModPForms.mem_modPMod_of_coe_mul_thetaJ_pow_eq_of_forall_ord_pos_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two).
